entry id and every enabled runtime id. Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill. The same block holds `COMMAND_POLICIES`, one policy per runnable string, so a surface that attaches a command can name its policy without a second lookup. It writes the `MODE_COMMANDS` block into the same file, one row per hub mode that names a command, and fails when a mode names a command with no file under `.skilled/commands/`. Each TypeScript bridge in `lib/scorer/projection.ts` carries an `ownerSkill`, the skill that owns its command. The generated JSON and generated source blocks are outputs, not hand-edited inputs.\nrg allow-list exit=1\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"COMMAND_ROWS\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md\\nrg -n \\\"allow-list.json\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md; echo \\\"rg allow-list exit=$?\\\"\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529136954,"end":1794529139179}}}}
